    "title": "Eye on the U: Miami Hurricanes are 5-0 but reeling with injuries - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan McPherson ,\n10 hours ago Miami Hurricanes Head Coach Mario Cristobal communicates with players in the game with Clemson during the second quarter at Memorial Stadium Saturday, October 3, 2026. Ken Ruinard / USA Today Network/USA TODAY Network via Reuters Co After a few weeks away, Eye on the U is back.\nThe Miami Hurricanes, meanwhile, keep rolling.\nThe Hurricanes are a perfect 5-0 and 3-0 in Atlantic Coast Conference play as they enter their bye week — a needed break from the schedule despite the dominant start.\nWhy needed? Because the team is dealing with a rash of injuries to key players, and the week without a game gives the Hurricanes a chance to recover before the long haul of the season that remains.\nOn this week's episode of Eye on the U, Miami Herald beat writer Jordan McPherson takes a look at Miami's 5-0 start, what stood out in last week’s win over Clemson and where things stand with the team as the second half of the schedule approaches.\n1",
